  "domain": "artificial-intelligence",
  "definition": "Homomorphic Encryption for Machine Learning is a cryptographic paradigm that enables arithmetic computations to be performed directly on ciphertext, so that AI model training and inference can proceed on encrypted data without any decryption step, guaranteeing that neither cloud servers nor third parties ever observe plaintext inputs, intermediate activations, or model weights. The approach relies on algebraic homomorphisms\u2014addition and multiplication over encrypted values\u2014combined with bootstrapping techniques to manage noise accumulation, with schemes such as CKKS targeting approximate real-number arithmetic well-suited to neural-network workloads. Applications span privacy-preserving inference, encrypted federated learning aggregation, and collaborative multi-party model training on sensitive data spanning healthcare, finance, and government.",
